{"name":"Blue Palisade","hex":"#01546d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"palisade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, strong stake, one end of which is set firmly in the ground, and the other sharpened.","A wall of wooden stakes, used as a defensive barrier."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To equip with a palisade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palisade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Palisade","blocks":[{"text":"A palisade, sometimes called a stakewall or a paling, is typically a row of closely placed, high vertical standing tree trunks or wooden or iron stakes used as a fence for enclosure or as a defensive wall. Palisades can form a stockade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/St_Fagans_Celtic_village_palisade.jpg/330px-St_Fagans_Celtic_village_palisade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palisade","wikidata":"Q90685"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG/500px-Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG/500px-Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reconstruction of a medieval palisade in Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg/500px-Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg/500px-Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Kincaid site, a Mississippian culture palisaded settlement in southern Illinois","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Angel_palisade_wall_and_bastions_HRoe_2008.jpg/500px-Angel_palisade_wall_and_bastions_HRoe_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Angel_palisade_wall_and_bastions_HRoe_2008.jpg/500px-Angel_palisade_wall_and_bastions_HRoe_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A section of reconstruc